@startuml Address_Complete_Flow_Sequence
!theme plain
title Tech Challenge - Fluxos Completos de Gestão de Endereços

' Definição de cores para cada camada
!define DRIVING_ADAPTER_COLOR #E8F5E8
!define APPLICATION_CORE_COLOR #E3F2FD  
!define DRIVEN_ADAPTER_COLOR #FFF3E0
!define DATABASE_COLOR #F3E5F5

actor "Cliente/Postman" as Client #FFE0B2

' Camada de Adaptadores de Entrada (Driving Adapters)
box "Driving Adapters" DRIVING_ADAPTER_COLOR
    participant "AddressController" as Controller
    participant "GlobalExceptionHandler" as ExceptionHandler
    participant "JwtAuthenticationFilter" as JwtFilter
    participant "AddressWebMapper" as WebMapper
end box

' Núcleo da Aplicação (Application Core)
box "Application Core" APPLICATION_CORE_COLOR
    participant "AddressCreatePort" as IAddressCreatePort
    participant "CreateAddressUseCase" as CreateAddressUC
    participant "AddressFindByUserPort" as IAddressFindPort
    participant "FindAddressUseCase" as FindAddressUC
    participant "AddressUpdatePort" as IAddressUpdatePort
    participant "UpdateAddressUseCase" as UpdateAddressUC
    participant "AddressDeletePort" as IAddressDeletePort
    participant "DeleteAddressUseCase" as DeleteAddressUC
    participant "AddressRepositoryPort" as IAddressRepo
    participant "AddressDomainService" as AddressDomainService
    participant "AddressDomain" as AddressEntity
end box

' Camada de Adaptadores de Saída (Driven Adapters)
box "Driven Adapters" DRIVEN_ADAPTER_COLOR
    participant "AddressRepositoryImpl" as RepoAdapter
    participant "JpaAddressRepository" as JpaRepo
    participant "AddressEntityMapper" as AddressMapper
end box

' Infraestrutura de Dados
box "Database" DATABASE_COLOR
    database "PostgreSQL" as DB
end box

== Cenário 1: Criar Endereço ==

Client -> Controller : POST /api/v1/address\n{ "street": "Rua das Flores", "number": "123", ... }
activate Controller

note right of Controller
    AddressCreateRequestDTO:
    - street, number, complement
    - neighborhood, city, zipCode
    + Authentication: Bearer token
end note

Controller -> WebMapper : toApplicationRequest(dto, userId)
activate WebMapper
WebMapper --> Controller : AddressCreateRequest
deactivate WebMapper

Controller -> IAddressCreatePort : createAddress(request)
activate IAddressCreatePort

IAddressCreatePort -> CreateAddressUC : createAddress(request)
activate CreateAddressUC

CreateAddressUC -> AddressEntity : create(userId, street, number, ...)
activate AddressEntity
note right of AddressEntity
    Factory Method:
    - Validates all fields
    - Creates domain entity
    - Sets createdAt timestamp
end note
AddressEntity --> CreateAddressUC : AddressDomain
deactivate AddressEntity

CreateAddressUC -> IAddressRepo : save(addressDomain)
activate IAddressRepo

IAddressRepo -> RepoAdapter : save(addressDomain)
activate RepoAdapter

RepoAdapter -> AddressMapper : toJpaEntity(addressDomain)
activate AddressMapper
AddressMapper --> RepoAdapter : JpaAddressEntity
deactivate AddressMapper

RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo : save(jpaEntity)
activate JpaRepo
JpaRepo -> DB : INSERT INTO address VALUES(...)
activate DB
DB --> JpaRepo : address record saved
deactivate DB
JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter : JpaAddressEntity (with ID)
deactivate JpaRepo

RepoAdapter -> AddressMapper : toDomain(jpaEntity)
activate AddressMapper
AddressMapper --> RepoAdapter : AddressDomain
deactivate AddressMapper

RepoAdapter --> IAddressRepo : AddressDomain
deactivate RepoAdapter

IAddressRepo --> CreateAddressUC : AddressDomain
deactivate IAddressRepo

CreateAddressUC -> CreateAddressUC : AddressMapper.toResponse(addressDomain)
CreateAddressUC --> IAddressCreatePort : AddressResponse
deactivate CreateAddressUC

IAddressCreatePort --> Controller : AddressResponse
deactivate IAddressCreatePort

Controller -> WebMapper : toResponseDTO(response)
activate WebMapper
WebMapper --> Controller : AddressResponseDTO
deactivate WebMapper

Controller --> Client : 201 Created\n{ "id": "uuid", "street": "Rua das Flores", ... }
deactivate Controller

== Cenário 2: Listar Endereços do Usuário ==

Client -> Controller : GET /api/v1/address
activate Controller

Controller -> IAddressFindPort : findAddress(userId)
activate IAddressFindPort

IAddressFindPort -> FindAddressUC : findAddress(userId)
activate FindAddressUC

FindAddressUC -> IAddressRepo : findByAddressFromUser(userId)
activate IAddressRepo

IAddressRepo -> RepoAdapter : findByAddressFromUser(userId)
activate RepoAdapter

RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo : findByUserId(userId)
activate JpaRepo
JpaRepo -> DB : SELECT * FROM address WHERE user_id = ?
activate DB
DB --> JpaRepo : List<JpaAddressEntity>
deactivate DB
JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter : List<JpaAddressEntity>
deactivate JpaRepo

RepoAdapter -> AddressMapper : toDomainList(jpaEntities)
activate AddressMapper
AddressMapper --> RepoAdapter : List<AddressDomain>
deactivate AddressMapper

RepoAdapter --> IAddressRepo : List<AddressDomain>
deactivate RepoAdapter

IAddressRepo --> FindAddressUC : List<AddressDomain>
deactivate IAddressRepo

FindAddressUC -> FindAddressUC : AddressMapper.toResponseList(domains)
FindAddressUC --> IAddressFindPort : List<AddressResponse>
deactivate FindAddressUC

IAddressFindPort --> Controller : List<AddressResponse>
deactivate IAddressFindPort

Controller -> WebMapper : toResponseDTOList(responses)
activate WebMapper
WebMapper --> Controller : List<AddressResponseDTO>
deactivate WebMapper

Controller --> Client : 200 OK\n[{ "id": "uuid1", ... }, { "id": "uuid2", ... }]
deactivate Controller

== Cenário 3: Atualizar Endereço ==

Client -> Controller : PUT /api/v1/address/{addressId}\n{ "street": "Rua Nova", ... }
activate Controller

Controller -> WebMapper : toApplicationUpdateRequest(dto)
activate WebMapper
WebMapper --> Controller : AddressUpdateRequest
deactivate WebMapper

Controller -> IAddressUpdatePort : updateAddress(userId, addressId, request)
activate IAddressUpdatePort

IAddressUpdatePort -> UpdateAddressUC : updateAddress(userId, addressId, request)
activate UpdateAddressUC

UpdateAddressUC -> AddressDomainService : ensureAddressBelongsToUser(userId, addressId)
activate AddressDomainService

AddressDomainService -> IAddressRepo : findById(addressId)
activate IAddressRepo
IAddressRepo -> RepoAdapter : findById(addressId)
activate RepoAdapter
RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo : findById(addressId)
activate JpaRepo
JpaRepo -> DB : SELECT * FROM address WHERE id = ?
activate DB
DB --> JpaRepo : JpaAddressEntity
deactivate DB
JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter : Optional<JpaAddressEntity>
deactivate JpaRepo
RepoAdapter -> AddressMapper : toDomain(jpaEntity)
activate AddressMapper
AddressMapper --> RepoAdapter : AddressDomain
deactivate AddressMapper
RepoAdapter --> IAddressRepo : Optional<AddressDomain>
deactivate RepoAdapter
IAddressRepo --> AddressDomainService : Optional<AddressDomain>
deactivate IAddressRepo

alt Address belongs to user
    AddressDomainService --> UpdateAddressUC : validation OK
    deactivate AddressDomainService
    
    UpdateAddressUC -> IAddressRepo : findById(addressId)
    activate IAddressRepo
    IAddressRepo --> UpdateAddressUC : AddressDomain
    deactivate IAddressRepo
    
    UpdateAddressUC -> AddressEntity : updateInfo(street, number, ...)
    activate AddressEntity
    note right of AddressEntity
        Business Method:
        - Validates new data
        - Updates entity fields  
        - Sets updatedAt timestamp
    end note
    AddressEntity --> UpdateAddressUC : void
    deactivate AddressEntity
    
    UpdateAddressUC -> IAddressRepo : save(updatedAddress)
    activate IAddressRepo
    IAddressRepo -> RepoAdapter : save(addressDomain)
    activate RepoAdapter
    RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo : save(jpaEntity)
    activate JpaRepo
    JpaRepo -> DB : UPDATE address SET ... WHERE id = ?
    activate DB
    DB --> JpaRepo : updated record
    deactivate DB
    JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter : JpaAddressEntity
    deactivate JpaRepo
    RepoAdapter --> IAddressRepo : AddressDomain
    deactivate RepoAdapter
    IAddressRepo --> UpdateAddressUC : AddressDomain
    deactivate IAddressRepo
    
    UpdateAddressUC -> UpdateAddressUC : AddressMapper.toResponse(updatedAddress)
    UpdateAddressUC --> IAddressUpdatePort : AddressResponse
    deactivate UpdateAddressUC
    
    IAddressUpdatePort --> Controller : AddressResponse
    deactivate IAddressUpdatePort
    
    Controller -> WebMapper : toResponseDTO(response)
    activate WebMapper
    WebMapper --> Controller : AddressResponseDTO
    deactivate WebMapper
    
    Controller --> Client : 200 OK\n{ "id": "uuid", "street": "Rua Nova", ... }
    deactivate Controller
    
else Address doesn't belong to user
    AddressDomainService -> AddressDomainService : throw AddresDoesNotBelongToUserException
    AddressDomainService --> UpdateAddressUC : Exception
    deactivate AddressDomainService
    
    UpdateAddressUC --> IAddressUpdatePort : Exception
    deactivate UpdateAddressUC
    
    IAddressUpdatePort --> Controller : Exception
    deactivate IAddressUpdatePort
    
    Controller -> ExceptionHandler : handle(AddresDoesNotBelongToUserException)
    activate ExceptionHandler
    ExceptionHandler --> Controller : 403 Forbidden
    deactivate ExceptionHandler
    
    Controller --> Client : 403 Forbidden\n{ "error": "Address does not belong to user" }
    deactivate Controller
end

== Cenário 4: Excluir Endereço ==

Client -> Controller : DELETE /api/v1/address/{addressId}
activate Controller

Controller -> IAddressDeletePort : deleteAddress(userId, addressId)
activate IAddressDeletePort

IAddressDeletePort -> DeleteAddressUC : deleteAddress(userId, addressId)
activate DeleteAddressUC

DeleteAddressUC -> AddressDomainService : ensureAddressBelongsToUser(userId, addressId)
activate AddressDomainService

AddressDomainService -> IAddressRepo : findById(addressId)
activate IAddressRepo
IAddressRepo --> AddressDomainService : Optional<AddressDomain>
deactivate IAddressRepo

alt Address belongs to user
    AddressDomainService --> DeleteAddressUC : validation OK
    deactivate AddressDomainService
    
    DeleteAddressUC -> IAddressRepo : deleteAddress(addressId)
    activate IAddressRepo
    
    IAddressRepo -> RepoAdapter : deleteAddress(addressId)
    activate RepoAdapter
    
    RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo : deleteById(addressId)
    activate JpaRepo
    JpaRepo -> DB : DELETE FROM address WHERE id = ?
    activate DB
    DB --> JpaRepo : record deleted
    deactivate DB
    JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter : void
    deactivate JpaRepo
    
    RepoAdapter --> IAddressRepo : void
    deactivate RepoAdapter
    
    IAddressRepo --> DeleteAddressUC : void
    deactivate IAddressRepo
    
    DeleteAddressUC --> IAddressDeletePort : void
    deactivate DeleteAddressUC
    
    IAddressDeletePort --> Controller : void
    deactivate IAddressDeletePort
    
    Controller --> Client : 204 No Content
    deactivate Controller
    
else Address doesn't belong to user
    AddressDomainService -> AddressDomainService : throw AddresDoesNotBelongToUserException
    AddressDomainService --> DeleteAddressUC : Exception
    deactivate AddressDomainService
    
    DeleteAddressUC --> IAddressDeletePort : Exception
    deactivate DeleteAddressUC
    
    IAddressDeletePort --> Controller : Exception
    deactivate IAddressDeletePort
    
    Controller -> ExceptionHandler : handle(AddresDoesNotBelongToUserException)
    activate ExceptionHandler
    ExceptionHandler --> Controller : 403 Forbidden
    deactivate ExceptionHandler
    
    Controller --> Client : 403 Forbidden\n{ "error": "Address does not belong to user" }
    deactivate Controller
end

note over Client, DB
    **Fluxos de Address na Arquitetura Hexagonal:**
    
    **1. Separação de Responsabilidades:**
    - **AddressController**: Recebe requisições HTTP e delega
    - **AddressWebMapper**: Converte DTOs Web ↔ Application
    - **Use Cases**: Executam lógica de negócio específica
    - **AddressDomainService**: Valida regras de negócio (ownership)
    - **AddressDomain**: Entidade rica com validações e comportamentos
    
    **2. Padrões Implementados:**
    - **Factory Pattern**: AddressDomain.create() para criação
    - **Repository Pattern**: AddressRepositoryPort para persistência
    - **Domain Service**: AddressDomainService para validações complexas
    - **Mapper Pattern**: Conversões entre camadas
    
    **3. Segurança e Validações:**
    - **Ownership Validation**: Usuário só acessa seus endereços
    - **Domain Validation**: AddressDomain valida campos obrigatórios
    - **Exception Handling**: RFC-7807 Problem Details
    - **Authentication**: JWT token em todos os endpoints
    
    **4. Benefícios da Arquitetura:**
    - **Testabilidade**: Use Cases testáveis independentemente
    - **Desacoplamento**: Infraestrutura isolada do domínio
    - **Extensibilidade**: Novos adapters sem afetar core
    - **Manutenibilidade**: Responsabilidades bem definidas
end note

@enduml